{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST store persistent per-user activity state under\n`$XDG_STATE_HOME/habeas` on Unix when XDG_STATE_HOME is an absolute, nonempty path,\notherwise under `$HOME/.local/state/habeas`. On Windows it MUST use\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%/habeas/state`. `HOME` and `LOCALAPPDATA` MUST likewise be\nabsolute, nonempty paths to be used. Features MUST use a named subdirectory under that\nstate root and document their record formats and locations.\n\nState MUST persist across invocations and MUST NOT be stored in the project\nrepository, the configuration file, or a disposable cache directory. Habeas MUST\ncreate the required directories when recording state. If it cannot determine or\nwrite the state location, the operation requiring that state MUST report the\nfailure and MUST NOT claim that its history was recorded.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation of `requirements.configuration.state_location`.\n\n**Location selection**\n- `tests/configuration.rs#fn[locations_use_absolute_xdg_values_and_platform_fallbacks]` asserts `state_root_from` returns `$XDG_STATE_HOME/habeas` when the value is absolute and nonempty.\n- It also asserts the `$HOME/.local/state/habeas` fallback when XDG is empty or relative, and `%LOCALAPPDATA%/habeas/state` on Windows.\n- It asserts an error when Windows `LOCALAPPDATA` is missing.\n- `tests/configuration.rs#fn[base_directories_must_be_absolute_and_nonempty]` asserts errors that name `HOME` (Unix) or `LOCALAPPDATA` (Windows) when the value is empty or relative.\n- The same test asserts that a relative XDG value falls back to an absolute `HOME`.\n\n**Named subdirectory, record formats and locations**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` checks usage records land in `habeas/authoring/usage`.\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[closing_an_acknowledged_issue_makes_the_fixme_record_stale_and_reassessed]` checks GitHub cache files land in `habeas/github` (`habeas/state/github` on Windows).\n- `tests/configuration.rs#fn[configuration_documentation_covers_locations_structure_editing_and_removal]` checks `md/reference.md` for the usage and GitHub-cache locations and the cache record fields.\n- `tests/configuration.rs#fn[authoring_documentation_shows_each_configuration_task]` checks the authoring chapter for the usage-record format.\n\n**Persistence and directory creation**\n- The test fixtures give a `state` path that does not exist beforehand, so the successful runs also show that Habeas creates the required directories.\n- The usage test runs `author` twice and asserts the first record is byte-identical afterwards and that two records exist.\n- The GitHub cache test shows cached entries reused across invocations and removed only by the test.\n- `src/github.rs#mod[tests]/fn[results_are_cached_by_issue_for_an_hour_and_failures_are_not]` asserts cached entries are reused across reads and failures are not cached.\n\n**Not in the project repository**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[undeterminable_unwritable_or_project_state_fails_before_a_model_request]` and `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[state_reaching_the_project_through_a_symlink_is_refused]` cover a state root inside the project, a symlink to it, and a nonexistent path under such a symlink.\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[github_reads_do_not_cache_in_a_state_root_inside_the_project]` covers the same for GitHub reads. It asserts nothing is written, `status` reports \"cannot locate GitHub cache\", and `author` fails.\n- The exact-path assertions above establish that state goes under the state root rather than the configuration file or a cache directory. The text states no separate observable behavior for those two exclusions.\n\n**Failure reporting**\n- `fn[undeterminable_unwritable_or_project_state_fails_before_a_model_request]` covers an undeterminable location (`HOME` and XDG removed) and an uncreatable location (a regular file in the way). Each asserts a nonzero exit with an error and no model request.\n- `fn[usage_write_failures_are_reported_without_claiming_recorded_history]` makes the usage record unwritable. It asserts \"cannot record\" in stderr, a failing exit, and no usage summary on stdout.\n- `src/github.rs#mod[tests]/fn[cache_write_failures_are_reported_instead_of_returning_uncached_success]` asserts a `Failed` read with \"cannot record GitHub cache\" when the cache directory cannot be created.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap.",
